title: Inter-Party Relationships
new-page: true
view-if: inter_party_relationships_timer <= 0
tags: party_affairs
is-card: true
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; inter_party_relationships_timer = 6;
card-image: img/weimar_coalition_2.jpg
#subtitle: Building relations with the other political parties of the Commonwealth.

= Inter-Party Relationships

The <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> cannot govern by itself yet. Because we do not have an electoral majority, we need the support of other parties. Recently, our governments have consisted of the Unity Coalition of the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span>, <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>, and [? if ddp_name == "Gold" and not lvp_formed: <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**Democratic**</span>?][? if ddp_name == "DStP" and not lvp_formed: <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**State**</span>?][? if lvp_formed: <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>?] parties. [? if concord_formed: However the formation of the <span style="color: #000000;">**[+ unionist_party_name +]**</span> has only really made cooperation with the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">liberals</span> possible. ?] We can reach out and build additional connections with these parties, or perhaps we can stand alone.

- @liberals: Strengthen our bonds with the left-liberal [? if ddp_name == "Gold": <span style="color: #D3C24D;">Commonwealth Democratic Party</span>?][? if ddp_name == "DStP": <span style="color: #D3C24D;">Commonwealth State Party</span>?] and conservative-liberal <span style="color: #C0A054;">Commonwealth People's Party</span>.
- @liberals_ddp: Strengthen our bonds with the left-liberal [? if ddp_name == "Gold": <span style="color: #D3C24D;">Commonwealth Democratic Party</span>?][? if ddp_name == "DStP": <span style="color: #D3C24D;">Commonwealth State Party</span>?].
- @liberals_lvp: Strengthen our bonds with the <span style="color: #FFCC00;">Golds</span>.
- @center: Strengthen our bonds with the Catholic [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?].
- @cvp: Reconcile with the <span style="color: #000000;">Christian People's Party</span>.
- @kpd: Work towards repairing relationships with the <span style="color: #700000;">Communist Party</span>.
- @dnvp: Open dialogue with [? if traditionalist_leader != "Lambach": Trevannon and the <span style="color: #0087DC;">People's Conservatives</span>?][? if traditionalist_leader == "Lambach": Lambach and the <span style="color: #6D5298;">Christian Socials</span>?] of the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>.
- @nsdap: Establish contact with Crowde and the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalist Party</span>'s left wing.
- @spd_alone: The <span style="color: #c00000;">Marchers</span> can stand alone for now.
- @easy_discard


@kpd
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; collectivist_inter_party_seen += 1
go-to: kpd_blutmai if blutmai = 1; kpd_1 if blutmai = 0 and collectivist_coalition_success = 0 and (collectivist_relation < 40 or collectivist_rectifed_history = 1); kpd_rectification_of_history if collectivist_relation >= 40 and collectivist_rectified_history = 0; kpd_2 if collectivist_coalition_success = 1 and collectivist_rectified_history = 1

@kpd_1
on-arrival: collectivist_relation += 6*(1 - dissent); communist_coalition += 1 if collectivist_inter_party_seen <= 1; reformist_dissent += 2; unionist_relation -= 2 if unionist_ideology == "Right"; gold_relation -= 3; ddp_relation -= 2; lvp_relation -= 3

The <span style="color: #700000;">communists</span> are suspicious of our overtures, especially the <span style="color: #8B0000;">Stalinist</span> leadership, who persist in calling us "<span style="color: #c00000;">social</span> <span style="color: #7A3C00;">fascists</span>". However, connections are made at the grassroots and local levels.

@kpd_rectification_of_history

One stumbling block for our relations with the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> is our history of conflict, dating back to 1918 and 1919. The <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> is especially contemptuous of Gustav Brask, the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> "bloodhound" who reportedly ordered the violent suppression of the <span style="color: #700000;">Spartacist</span> uprising and other <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> revolts. They also blame us for the deaths of Rosa Luxemburg and Karl Liebknecht, two <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span>-turned-<span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> leaders who were killed during the suppression of the uprising.

For further improvements in <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> relations, it might be necessary to expel Brask, and hold some sort of commemoration for Luxemburg and Liebknecht.

- @yes_history: Yes, we must apologize for our past actions.
- @no_history: No, we have no need to apologize.

@yes_history
on-arrival: reformist_dissent += 12; reformist_strength -= 2; knight_dissent += 5; left_dissent -= 6; left_strength += 5; collectivist_rectified_history = 1; unionist_relation -= 3; unionist_relation -= 3 if unionist_ideology == "Right"; gold_relation -= 6; lvp_relation -= 6; ddp_relation -= 4; collectivist_relation += 8*(1-dissent); coalition_dissent += 1; gold_right += 2; ddp_right += 2; lvp_right += 2

As part of normalizing relations with the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span>, we have to acknowledge the wrongdoings of our past. We have expelled Brask, and have held public commemorations for those killed by troops during the uprisings.

This leads to tensions with the moderates and reformists within our party, and criticism from the <span style="color: #000000;">conservative</span> and <span style="color: #C0A054;">liberal</span> parties.

@no_history
on-arrival: collectivist_relation -= 3

We have no need to apologize for the actions of Ebert and Brask; it is the <span style="color: #700000;">communists</span>' fault for launching a violent insurrection.


@kpd_2
on-arrival: collectivist_relation += 8*(1 - dissent); communist_coalition += 1 if collectivist_inter_party_seen <= 1; reformist_dissent += 2; unionist_relation -= 3; gold_relation -= 3; lvp_relation -= 3; ddp_relation -= 3

After the success of the coalition government with the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span>, they are much more amenable to us.

@kpd_blutmai
on-arrival: collectivist_relation += 3*(1 - dissent); reformist_dissent += 1

After the events of Blütmai, reconciling with the <span style="color: #700000;">Communists</span> is difficult, if not impossible. Nevertheless, we must try.

@center
subtitle: -1 resources
view-if: not concord_formed
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; unionist_relation += 2 if unionist_ideology == "Left"
go-to: center_op if not marcher_in_government and chancellor != "Askew" and ((chancellor != "Goodryke" and chancellor != "Staal" and chancellor != "Goodlake") or (unionist_in_gov or unionist_in_gov_mini)); center_op_2 if not marcher_in_government and (chancellor == "Goodryke" or chancellor == "Staal") and not unionist_in_gov; center_coalition if marcher_in_government; center_bruning if chancellor = "Askew" and not marcher_in_government

@center_op
on-arrival: unionist_relation += 5*(1 - dissent)

We are currently in opposition to the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?]-led government, but that does not preclude the general building of feelings of good will.

@center_op_2
on-arrival: unionist_relation += 6*(1 - dissent)

Together with the <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>, we share a common opposition to the incumbent cabinet, making improving relations easier.

@center_coalition
on-arrival: unionist_relation += 8*(1 - dissent)

We are currently coalition partners with them, so improving relations comes naturally.

@center_bruning
on-arrival: unionist_relation += 5*(1 - dissent)

The Askew semi-<span style="color: #808080;">autocratic</span> regime makes building friendly relations difficult, but not impossible.

@cvp
subtitle: -1 resources
view-if: concord_formed
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; unionist_relation += 6*(1 - dissent); concord_left += 1

It's not exactly easy to get the <span style="color: #000000;">Christians</span> to like us again—but it's not impossible either. We will leverage our connections with their <span style="color: #FF7F00;">Christian Left</span> and Labor factions to lay the groundwork for a potential reconciliation between our two parties.

@liberals_ddp
view-if: not lvp_formed and not gold_exist
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; ddp_relation += 8*(1 - dissent); ddp_left += 1; ddp_cohesion += 0.5

The <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span> has been one of our closest allies throughout the course of the Republic. Now, as they are the only remaining liberal party, strengthening ties with them should be our top priority.

@liberals
view-if: not lvp_formed and gold_exist
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; ddp_relation += 5*(1 - dissent); ddp_left += 0.5; ddp_cohesion += 0.25; gold_relation += 2 if in_grand_coalition_heartland
go-to: dvp_stresemann if stresemann_dead = 0; dvp_loss if stresemann_dead = 1 and gold_votes >= 5; dvp_moribund if stresemann_dead = 1 and gold_votes < 5

The <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span> has been one of our closest allies through the course of the Republic. [? if year >= 1929: Although the national shift to the right is having them question our cooperation. ?]

@dvp_stresemann
on-arrival: gold_relation += 6*(1 - dissent); gold_left += 1; gold_left += 1 if in_grand_coalition_heartland

Gustav Stratton, the leader of the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> is the best foreign policy leaders of the republic, and while he has previously expressed <span style="color: #808080;">monarchist</span> tendencies, he has been friendly towards us. [? if in_grand_coalition_heartland: Their inclusion in the Heartland government has fostered a more conciliatory attitude toward us. ?]

@dvp_loss
on-arrival: gold_relation += 4*(1 - dissent); gold_left += 1; gold_left += 1 if in_grand_coalition_heartland

With the death of Gustav Stratton, the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> is much less likely to be accommodating of us. In addition, the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">liberal</span> parties are electorally in decline, so perhaps our efforts are best spent elsewhere.

However, given the influence of the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> among the other <span style="color: #808080;">right</span>-leaning parties[? if president == "DuFour" or president_ideology == "Moderate": and with President [+ president +] ?], it can still be helpful to influence them. [? if in_grand_coalition_heartland: Their inclusion in the Heartland government has also fostered a more conciliatory attitude toward us. ?]

@dvp_moribund
on-arrival: gold_relation += 4*(1 - dissent); gold_left += 1; gold_left += 1 if in_grand_coalition_heartland

The <span style="color: #D3C24D;">liberal</span> parties (both the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span> and <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>) are electorally <span style="color: #ff0000;">moribund</span>, so perhaps our efforts are best spent elsewhere.

However, given the influence of the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> among the other <span style="color: #808080;">right</span>-leaning parties[? if president == "DuFour" or president_ideology == "Moderate": and with President [+ president +] ?], it can still be helpful to influence them. [? if in_grand_coalition_heartland: Their inclusion in the Heartland government has also fostered a more conciliatory attitude toward us. ?]

@liberals_lvp
view-if: lvp_formed
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1
go-to: lvp_stresemann if stresemann_dead = 0; lvp_loss if stresemann_dead = 1

The former two liberal parties have been our closest allies through the course of the Republic. [? if year >= 1929: Although the national shift to the right is having them question our cooperation. ?]

@lvp_stresemann
on-arrival: lvp_relation += 6*(1 - dissent); lvp_left += 1

Gustav Stratton, the former leader of the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>, is the best foreign policy leaders of the republic, and while he has previously expressed <span style="color: #808080;">monarchist</span> tendencies, he has been friendly towards us. Stratton's influence over the right wing of the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> helps sway some more reluctant party members towards us.

@lvp_loss
on-arrival: lvp_relation += 4*(1 - dissent); lvp_left += 1

With the death of Gustav Stratton, the right wing of the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> is much less likely to be accommodating of us. In addition, the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">liberals</span> are electorally in decline, so perhaps our efforts are best spent elsewhere.

However, given the influence of the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> among the other <span style="color: #808080;">right</span>-leaning parties [? if president == "DuFour" or president_ideology == "Moderate": and with President [+ president +] ?], it can still be helpful to influence them. 

@dnvp
view-if: wacky_weimar
choose-if: resources >= 1 and ((traditionalist_leader == "Trevannon" and true_christian_democracy) or (traditionalist_leader == "Lambach" and lambach_stays))
unavailable-subtitle: [? if resources < 1: Not enough resources. ?] [? if traditionalist_leader != "Trevannon" and traditionalist_leader != "Lambach": Trevannon or Lambach must lead the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">Traditionalists</span>. ?][? if not true_christian_democracy and traditionalist_leader == "Trevannon": Trevannon's wholesomeness is restrained by his own party. ?][? if not lambach_stays and traditionalist_leader == "Lambach": Lambach's wholesomeness is restrained by his own party, he must consolidate his position first. ?]
on-arrival: resources -= 1; traditionalist_relation += 10*(1-dissent); pro_republic += 3; left_dissent += 10; center_dissent += 10

We have reached out to [+ traditionalist_leader +], who responds warmly to our requests. However, it would take much more convincing to get the evil and unwholesome side of the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> behind closer cooperation. Our Left and Center factions voice their disapproval.

- @dnvp_wholesome

@dnvp_wholesome
title: Conclude an electoral alliance with the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>.
choose-if: in_wholesome_coalition and lambach_stays and traditionalist_leader == "Lambach"
unavailable-subtitle: [? if traditionalist_leader != "Lambach" or not lambach_stays: Only Lambach can accept this deal after he has consolidated power. ?][? if not in_wholesome_coalition: We must be governing together. ?]
on-arrival: {!
Q.traditionalist_wholesome = 1; 

Q.wholesome_point += 1;

Q.burgher_ddp += 20;
Q.burgher_lvp += 20;

Q.commons_traditionalist = Q.commons_marcher;
Q.commons_marcher = Q.commons_traditionalist;

Q.burgher_traditionalist = Q.burgher_marcher;
Q.burgher_marcher = Q.burgher_traditionalist;

Q.guild_traditionalist = Q.guild_marcher;
Q.guild_marcher = Q.guild_traditionalist;

Q.landed_traditionalist = Q.landed_marcher;
Q.landed_marcher = Q.landed_traditionalist;

Q.faithful_traditionalist = Q.faithful_marcher;
Q.faithful_marcher = Q.faithful_traditionalist;

Q.disfavored_traditionalist = Q.disfavored_marcher;
Q.disfavored_marcher = Q.disfavored_traditionalist;

Q.unionist_minus_bvp_votes = parseFloat((Q.unionist_votes - Q.bvp_votes).toFixed(1));
Q.unionist_minus_bvp_r = parseFloat((Q.unionist_r - Q.bvp_r).toFixed(1));
if (Q.bvp_r == Q.unionist_r) Q.unionist_minus_bvp_r = 0;
!}
on-display: {!
data = [{
    "id": "collectivist",
    "legend": "Collectivist",
    "name": "Collectivist",
    "seats": Math.round(Q.collectivist_r * Q.reichstag_size),
}];

if (Q.sapd_formed && Q.sapd_r) {
    data.push({
        "id": "sapd",
        "legend": "SAPD",
        "name": "SAPD",
        "seats": Math.round(Q.sapd_r * Q.reichstag_size),
    });
}

if (Q.marcher_r) {
    data.push({
        "id": "marcher",
        "legend": "Marcher",
        "name": "Marcher",
        "seats": Math.round(Q.marcher_r * Q.reichstag_size),
    });
}

if (Q.rdp_r) {
    data.push({
        "id": "rdp",
        "legend": "RDP",
        "name": "RDP",
        "seats": Math.round(Q.rdp_r * Q.reichstag_size),
    });
}

if (Q.traditionalist_r && Q.traditionalist_wholesome) {
    data.push({
        "id": "traditionalist_wholesome",
        "legend": "Traditionalist",
        "name": "Traditionalist",
        "seats": Math.round(Q.traditionalist_r * Q.reichstag_size),
    });
}

if (Q.ddp_r && !Q.lvp_formed) {
    data.push({
        "id": "ddp",
        "legend": Q.ddp_name,
        "name": Q.ddp_name,
        "seats": Math.round(Q.ddp_r * Q.reichstag_size),
    });
}

if (Q.lvp_r && Q.lvp_formed) {
    data.push({
        "id": "lvp",
        "legend": "LVP",
        "name": "LVP",
        "seats": Math.round(Q.lvp_r * Q.reichstag_size),
    });
}

if (Q.unionist_minus_bvp_r) {
    data.push({
        "id": "unionist",
        "legend": "Center",
        "name": "Center",
        "seats": Math.round(Q.unionist_minus_bvp_r * Q.reichstag_size),
    });
}

if (Q.bvp_r) {
    data.push({
        "id": "bvp",
        "legend": "Arcanists",
        "name": "Arcanists",
        "seats": Math.round(Q.bvp_r * Q.reichstag_size),
    });
}

if (Q.gold_r && !Q.lvp_formed && Q.gold_exist) {
    data.push({
        "id": "gold",
        "legend": "Gold",
        "name": "Gold",
        "seats": Math.round(Q.gold_r * Q.reichstag_size),
    });
}

if (Q.gnu_r && Q.gnu_formed) {
    data.push({
        "id": "gnu",
        "legend": "GNU",
        "name": "GNU",
        "seats": Math.round(Q.gnu_r * Q.reichstag_size),
    });
}

if (Q.other_r) {
    data.push({
        "id": "other",
        "legend": "Other",
        "name": "Other",
        "seats": Math.round(Q.other_r * Q.reichstag_size),
    });
}

if (Q.kvp_formed && Q.kvp_r) {
    data.push({
        "id": "kvp",
        "legend": "KVP",
        "name": "KVP",
        "seats": Math.round(Q.kvp_r * Q.reichstag_size),
    });
}

if (Q.traditionalist_r && !Q.traditionalist_wholesome) {
    data.push({
        "id": "traditionalist",
        "legend": "Traditionalist",
        "name": "Traditionalist",
        "seats": Math.round(Q.traditionalist_r * Q.reichstag_size),
    });
}

if (Q.dnf_formed && Q.dnf_r) {
    data.push({
        "id": "dnf",
        "legend": "DNF",
        "name": "DNF",
        "seats": Math.round(Q.dnf_r * Q.reichstag_size),
    });
}

if (Q.dsu_exist && Q.dsu_r) {
    data.push({
        "id": "dsu",
        "legend": "DSU",
        "name": "DSU",
        "seats": Math.round(Q.dsu_r * Q.reichstag_size),
    });
}

if (Q.royalist_split && Q.royalist_gallax_r) {
    data.push({
        "id": "royalist",
        "legend": "Royalist",
        "name": "Royalist",
        "seats": Math.round(Q.royalist_gallax_r * Q.reichstag_size),
    });
}

if (!Q.royalist_split && Q.royalist_r) {
    data.push({
        "id": "royalist",
        "legend": "Royalist",
        "name": "Royalist",
        "seats": Math.round(Q.royalist_r * Q.reichstag_size),
    });
}

if (Q.nvf_exist && Q.nvf_r) {
    data.push({
        "id": "nvf",
        "legend": "NVF",
        "name": "NVF",
        "seats": Math.round(Q.nvf_r * Q.reichstag_size),
    });
}
if (d3 && window) {
    // get screen width
    var width = 500;
    var height = 500;
    var screenWidth = document.getElementById('content').offsetWidth;
    if (screenWidth < width - 50) {
        width = screenWidth - 50;
        height = width;
        document.getElementById("reichstag").style.height = screenWidth/2 + "px";
    }
    var parliament = d3.parliament();
    parliament.width(width).height(height).innerRadiusCoef(0.4);
    parliament.enter.fromCenter(true).smallToBig(true);
    parliament.exit.toCenter(false).bigToSmall(true);
    d3.select("#reichstag").datum(data).call(parliament);
}
!}


Due to our shared values of wholesomeness and love, we have agreed to run a joint list with the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> and welcome them into our parliamentary group. However, because of this deal, we had to expel all our <span style="color: #005EB8;">Jewish</span> members, who join the [? if not lvp_formed: <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span>?][? if lvp_formed: <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>?].

{!<svg id="reichstag" style="width: 500px; height: 250px;"> </svg>!}

@nsdap
view-if: wacky_weimar
choose-if: resources >= 1 and saxony_royalist
unavailable-subtitle: [? if resources < 1: Not enough resources. ?] [? if not saxony_royalist: Gregor Crowde have a position in the Dornish state government in order to wholesomeify him via governmental participation. ?]
on-arrival: resources -= 1; royalist_relation += 10*(1-dissent); pro_republic += 3; left_dissent += 10; center_dissent += 10

We have began our work in wholesomeifying Gregor Crowde, who is beginning to form a moderate pro-democratic <span style="color: #7A3C00;">National Reformist</span> faction within the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span> under Gallax's nose. Our Left and Center factions voice their disapproval.

- @nsdap_wholesome
- @nsdap_wholesome_2

@nsdap_wholesome
title: Create the anti-Liberal Front.
unavailable-subtitle: [? if royalist_relation < 50: We need higher relations. ?][? if harzburg_front_seen: The Harzburg Front already exists. ?]
choose-if: royalist_relation >= 50 and not harzburg_front_seen
on-arrival: commons_ddp = 0; burgher_ddp = 0; guild_ddp = 0; landed_ddp = 0; faithful_ddp = 0; disfavored_ddp = 0; commons_gold = 0; burgher_gold = 0; guild_gold = 0; landed_gold = 0; faithful_gold = 0; disfavored_gold = 0; commons_lvp = 0; burgher_lvp = 0; guild_lvp = 0; landed_lvp = 0; faithful_lvp = 0; disfavored_lvp = 0; ddp_relation = 0; lvp_relation = 0; gold_relation = 0; unionist_relation += 20; traditionalist_relation += 20

We have formed the anti-Liberal front with Crowde's faction within the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span>. The [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] and <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> also join in.

@nsdap_wholesome_2
title: Merge the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Iron**</span> <span style="color: #1A1A1A;">**Front**</span> and the Harzburg Front.
unavailable-subtitle: [? if royalist_relation < 50: We need higher relations. ?][? if not harzburg_front_seen: The Harzburg Front hasn't been invented yet. ?]
choose-if: royalist_relation >= 50 and harzburg_front_seen
on-arrival: banner_strength += loyalist_strength; banner_strength += warden_strength; banner_militancy += 0.5; loyalist_strength = 0; warden_strength = 0

The <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Wardens**</span> and <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**SA**</span> has dissolved and joined the the Banners!

@spd_alone

Whether it is because we *cannot* or *will not*, we do not make ties with other parties at this moment.

- @return: Continue...
